Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] csvsplit: fix heap-buffer-overflow in copy_quoted()

AddressSanitizer reports a heap-buffer-overflow in copy_quoted()
(src/csvsplit.c:33).

The change, in src/csvsplit.c:

    -    char *field = malloc(inner); /* room for the content */
    +    char *field = malloc(inner + 1); /* room for the content and NUL terminator */
---
 src/csvsplit.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/csvsplit.c b/src/csvsplit.c
--- a/src/csvsplit.c
+++ b/src/csvsplit.c
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
  * quote, `n` counts every byte up to and including the closing quote. */
 static char *copy_quoted(const char *raw, size_t n) {
     size_t inner = n >= 2 ? n - 2 : 0;
-    char *field = malloc(inner); /* room for the content */
+    char *field = malloc(inner + 1); /* room for the content and NUL terminator */
     size_t out = 0;
     if (field == NULL) {
         return NULL;
--
leakproof package
